@meta
id: 22-12
title: A column, not a line
chapter: 22
type: lesson
skills: visual-block
par: 19
minutes: 4
vscode: Alt+click on each line, Shift+Right twice, Delete
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
The third visual mode is the one VS Code has no real equivalent for.
`Ctrl-V` starts a block: a rectangle, so many columns wide and so many
lines tall, with the cursor at one corner. `j` makes it taller, `l`
makes it wider, and an operator acts on the rectangle — every line, but
only between those two columns.

The six lines in `cancel` were commented out for a deploy that is now
done. Uncomment them. The `// ` is three characters wide and sits in
the same column on every line, which is exactly the shape a block is
for.

@keys
| `Ctrl-V` | start a block selection |
| `j` `l` | grow the block down and right |
| `d` | delete the block on every line |

@hints
Get the cursor onto the first `/` of the first commented line. That is
the top-left corner.
--
`Ctrl-V`, then five `j` to reach the sixth line and two `l` to make it
three wide. The highlight is a rectangle, not a run of lines.
--
`/\/\/` `Enter`, `Ctrl-V`, `5j`, `2l`, `d`.

@solution
    /\/\/<Enter> Ctrl-V 5 j 2 l d :wq<Enter>

Sixteen keystrokes. Chapter 15 would do this with `:g/\/\//normal 3x`
or a substitute, and both are fine. The block is worth learning
anyway, because it is the only one of the three that carries into the
next lessons: insert on every line, append to every line, change a
column. `:g` cannot see columns. A block is nothing but columns.

Note that `2l` made the block three wide, not two: the cursor column
counts. If you overshoot, `h` shrinks it back; if you started at the
wrong corner, `O` swaps you to the other side.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    // if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
    //   throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    // }
    // if (order.status === 'CANCELLED') {
    //   return order;
    // }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }
    if (order.status === 'CANCELLED') {
      return order;
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
